The user wants to change the title of issue WEB-1 to "Checkout button broken on Safari". The Linear API is GraphQL-based. I need to find the issue by identifier (WEB-1) and update it.

First, I can query the issue by identifier to get its ID. The `issue` query gets a single issue by ID, but it might also support identifier. Let me try querying with identifier first.

I'll make a GraphQL query like:

```graphql
query {
  issue(identifier: "WEB-1") {
    id
    identifier
    title
  }
}
```

Then, I'll use the ID to update it:

```graphql
mutation {
  issueUpdate(input: {id: "...", title: "Checkout button broken on Safari"}) {
    success
    issue { id title }
  }
}
```

Let me start with the query first.

